; Monk research uses persistent package demand plus capability-local bounded cooldown. A failed research start clears only the claim and package; strategic monk demand remains valid for later reevaluation.
; University research uses capability-local cooldown and persistent package demand.
; Each technology owns its own failure budget. The existing 30-second
; fairness timer remains cooldown only, never a retry scheduler.
; Archery Range research uses persistent package demand plus capability-local bounded cooldown. Crossbow, Elite Skirmisher, and Arbalest re-enter after cooldown when their strategic predicates remain valid.
; Blacksmith research uses capability-local cooldown.
; Each technology owns a finite failed-start budget. The shared research
; failure timer remains cooldown/fairness state only.
; Stable, Siege, and Barracks research use persistent demand plus capability-local bounded cooldown. Failure never destroys a still-valid technology reason.
; Economic research uses persistent demand plus capability-local bounded cooldown. The shared failure timer is fairness state only.
; Gold Shaft Mining economic research bounded-start retry state.
; It is deliberately separate from Gold Mining because Shaft Mining has its
; own Castle BOOM strategic owner and must preserve demand across a failed
; research start without confusing it with Gold Mining demand.
(defconst bt-gold-shaft-mining-demand-goal 687)
; Castle Cataphract research uses persistent premium demand plus capability-local bounded cooldown.

